        "original_id": "df60ccad-dbed-5845-93fe-b3ee4be54599",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rebecca Forstadt, Reba West, John Pasquin, Tim Allen\n- Works: Code Geass, Metropolis, Antz, Dr. Dolittle, The Santa Clause, The Santa Clause trilogy, Masked Rider\n- Roles: voice actress, director, actor\n- Topics: anime, animated series, live-action shows, commercials, radio work, background voices\n\nFacts:\n- Rebecca Lynn Forstadt was born on December 16, 1953.\n- Rebecca Lynn Forstadt is also known as Reba West.\n- Rebecca Lynn Forstadt is an American voice actress best known for playing young female roles in various animated series.\n- The Santa Clause is a 1994 American Christmas fantasy family comedy film.\n- John Pasquin directed The Santa Clause.\n- The Santa Clause is the first installment in The Santa Clause trilogy.\n- Tim Allen stars in The Santa Clause as Scott Calvin, an ordinary man who accidentally causes Santa Claus to fall from his roof on Christmas Eve.\n- Rebecca Forstadt has voiced hundreds of anime characters, including Nunnally Lamperouge in Code Geass and Tima in Metropolis.\n- Rebecca Forstadt also worked in non-anime cartoons, live-action shows such as Masked Rider, commercials, and radio.\n- Rebecca Forstadt performed background voices for films including Antz, Dr. Dolittle, and The Santa Clause.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
